# HTTPD 4.0.0 Configuration
#
# Copy to SYS2.PARMLIB(HTTPPRM0)
# Referenced by HTTPPRM DD in the STC JCL procedure.
#
# Format: KEY=VALUE (case-insensitive keys)
# Lines starting with # or * are comments.
#
# --- Network ---
# PORT=8080
# BIND_TRIES=10
# BIND_SLEEP=10
# LISTEN_QUEUE=5
#
# --- Worker threads ---
# MINTASK=3
# MAXTASK=9
# CLIENT_TIMEOUT=10
#
# --- Keep-Alive ---
# KEEPALIVE_TIMEOUT=5
# KEEPALIVE_MAX=100
#
# --- Security ---
# LOGIN is the GLOBAL default for routes that set no explicit AUTH= (below).
# LOGIN=NONE
#
# Per-route auth policy -- trailing options on MOD= and LOC= override LOGIN:
#   AUTH=NONE|FORM|BASIC|TOKEN   RES=class:resource
#   RES=class:resource     optional RACF/RAKF resource check (READ)
#
# AUTH= does NOT select which credentials are accepted -- every route accepts
# all of them (Sec-Token/LtpaToken2 cookie, Bearer, Basic), because they are
# resolved before the route is even matched.  AUTH= selects WHETHER the route
# needs a login and HOW an unauthenticated request is challenged:
#   NONE    public, never challenged
#   FORM    the interactive HTML login form
#   BASIC   401 + WWW-Authenticate, so a browser pops its native dialog
#   TOKEN   a bare 401, never a challenge -- for APIs (see below)
#
# Use TOKEN wherever the client is a program that handles the 401 itself: a
# SPA using fetch/XHR, Zowe, curl scripts.  A WWW-Authenticate would make the
# browser pop its credential dialog, and the Basic credentials it then caches
# outlive the token session and defeat logout.  TOKEN still authenticates
# `curl -u user:pass` normally; it only stops advertising that it would.
# A route without AUTH= inherits the LOGIN default.  /login, /logout and the
# login-page assets stay reachable so an AUTH=FORM challenge can render.
#
# --- Storage lifetime for modules (no configuration) ---
# Every MOD= module runs with its heap in a request subpool: when the module
# abends, httpd releases the subpool in one FREEMAIN, so the cost of an abend
# is bounded by the request instead of by the life of the address space.
# There is nothing to configure.  The rule a module must follow:
#
#     malloc() is request storage.  Storage that must outlive the request
#     is obtained with __getmsp(size, 0)  (clibos.h).
#
# The retired RECLAIM= route option is accepted and ignored with a warning.
#
# --- UFS Filesystem ---
# DOCROOT=/www
#
# --- Debug ---
# DEBUG=0
#
# --- Modules ---
# Format: MOD=PROGRAM /url/pattern   (URL prefix match)
#         MOD=PROGRAM *.ext          (explicit extension - uses DOCROOT)
#         MOD=PROGRAM                (extension derived from module name,
#                                     e.g. MOD=LUA -> *.lua, MOD=REXX -> *.rexx)
#         any MOD= may add trailing  AUTH=mode  and/or  RES=class:resource
#
# Public z/OSMF endpoints must precede the gated /zosmf/* catch-all (first
# match wins): the anonymous reachability probe (/zosmf/info) and the token
# login/logout endpoint (/zosmf/services/authenticate) do their own auth, so
# the gate must not challenge them.
MOD=MVSMF /zosmf/info                    AUTH=NONE
MOD=MVSMF /zosmf/services/authenticate   AUTH=NONE
MOD=MVSMF /zosmf/*
# MOD=MVSMF /zosmf/*  AUTH=TOKEN RES=FACILITY:MVSMF.ACCESS  (protected API)
# MOD=HTTPDSRV /.dsrv  AUTH=FORM                             (browser login)
# MOD=HTTPDM /.dm
# MOD=HTTPDMTT /.dmtt
#
# ABEND0C1 allocates (?kb=n, default 128) and then abends S0C1 without freeing
# -- the acceptance probe for the storage reclaim.  Drive it a few hundred
# times and every other CGI must still load at its original speed.  Commented
# out: this is a diagnostic, not something to leave reachable.
# MOD=ABEND0C1 /.abend       AUTH=BASIC
#
# --- Static locations (LOC=) ---
# A path prefix WITHOUT a program: served statically from DOCROOT but still
# carrying the same AUTH=/RES= policy as MOD=.  Paths match exactly unless
# wildcarded (use a trailing *), and routes are tested in order, so list
# specific prefixes before a catch-all.
# LOC=/admin/*  AUTH=BASIC RES=FACILITY:HTTPD.ADMIN  (static area, profile)
# LOC=/*        AUTH=NONE                             (public SPA docroot)
#
# --- SMF Recording ---
# SMF=NONE|ERROR|AUTH|ALL [TYPE=nnn]
#   NONE  - no SMF recording (default)
#   ERROR - write SMF on HTTP errors (resp >= 400)
#   AUTH  - write on auth events (401/403) and errors
#   ALL   - every request (subtype 1) + session close (subtype 2)
#   TYPE  - SMF record type (128-255, default 243)
# SMF=NONE
# SMF=ALL TYPE=200
